espondents  around 40 percent would like to  increasingly automate payment process  and see the need for a programmable euro  in industry here  the keyword here is m2m payment i  machined two machine payments on the  internet  only 11 believe that a digital euro  would have no advantages at all  alongside the advocates of the digital  age however there are also skeptics  about the introduction of a digital euro  65 or around two-thirds see data  protection risk here if the central bank  were to gain deeper insights into our  payment processes  around one in two companies also see  this as a threat to financial stability  after all issuing the digital euro could  reduce the influence of banks in times  of crisis  but only three percent of banks and  financial service providers think  nothing of the ecb issuing a digital  euro around eight percent of the economy  as a whole believe that the economy  should develop its own solutions for the  payment transactions of the future  13 say there is nothing to be said  against a digital euro  thus 35 of the banking and financial  business are in favor of the  introduction of a digital euro in  assessment of the tendency 46 would  rather agree to a digital euro and only  9 clearly says no in any case the ecb is  determined to introduce a digital euro  the so-called euro this is to be issued  in parallel to cash which is  expressively not to be abolished  this is the ecb's response to numerous  new forms of payment such as crypto  assets like bitcoin liam or china's  euron  ecb president lagarde expects the euro  to be in the virtual wallets of eurozone  consumers in as little as four years and  then to be in heavy use  china is far ahead in the development of  a digital currency and sweden's central  bank is also working on the digital  corner what the euro will look like in  the end is not yet known not even by the  monetary guardians  but this much is already clear the  digital euro will be issued and  controlled by the ecb just like cash  like coins bills or book money in  checking or saving accounts it will be  created by the ecb and commercial banks  unlike bitcoin and other crypto assets  the central bank thus retains control  over the currency which is intended to  guarantee the stability and security of  the digital euro  the euro is to be stored in the kind of  virtual wallet and move into the  seller's virtual cache registered by  means of simple procedure for example  through an app or a qr code  this will be possible online via the  internet for example as well as offline  via bluetooth  in the future it will be much easier and  faster to make a payment than before via  scpa bank transfer  the whole thing will work via separate  account a direct account with the ecb so  to speak but still managed by the  commercial banks thus the euro is still  protected by the ecb even if private  financial institutions get into  difficulties due to a crises  privacy is also increasingly assured  because unlike major u.s credit card  companies no personal data is  transmitted during the transaction  on july 14th the council of the european  central bank decided to launch the  digital euro project  a lot of analysis have been done  feedback from citizens as well as  experts have been gathered  and the practical trial has been  conducted  with encouraging results  all of this has made it possible to  launch the digital euro project and who  knows maybe in four years we will be  shopping with the digital euro as  naturally as we do with credit card or  debit cards  the ecb and the euro area are well on  their way to bringing our financial  system into the digital age in a  controlled and secure manner  the digital euro will be the next step  into the future for europe and its  citizens  [Music]  you
 

